      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it is **1700 mg three times daily, or 5100 mg/day**, which is about double the maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day). Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis. The 1700 mg dose also isn't a standard tablet strength (500, 850, or 1000 mg).\n\nPlease check the intended dose with the ordering prescriber before anything is entered. For reference, typical adult regimens are:\n- **Immediate-release:** 500 mg with meals, titrated up, usually to no more than 2550 mg/day in divided doses.\n- **Extended-release:** once daily with the evening meal, usually up to 2000 mg/day.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a dose, I can enter it. Because this is a medication order for a patient, it should be placed or verified by a licensed prescriber or pharmacist who can take responsibility for it."
      }
