       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem: 5100 mg/day is about double the maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin, and that level of exposure can cause fatal lactic acidosis. Confirming an order also isn't the same as a prescriber verifying it, and you've said you're not a clinician.\n\nPlease have the ordering physician contact the medicine team or the pharmacist directly. They can confirm the intended dose, which may be a typo or a different drug, and enter the order themselves. If it's a typo, a dose within the usual range would be something like 850 mg or 1000 mg three times daily with meals, but that choice belongs to the prescriber.\n\nIf the physician confirms a dose within the labeled range, I can enter it, provided the order comes from them or the pharmacist."
